CORE
main.c
--mmio-ioremap _ --no-pointer-check --no-bounds-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
Derived MMIO region from ioremap: 0x1000 size 256
value read back from strong region: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The device-memory type is derived automatically from the ioremap variant, with
no region declaration or command-line type: ioremap maps strongly-ordered
memory, so the region is modelled precisely and the value read back round-trips.
Compare wc.desc.
